WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:15.387
Miss Minchin disliked Sara.

2
00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:19.061
But the headmistress didn't want to make Sara unhappy.

3
00:00:19.062 --> 00:00:23.934
If that happened, Sara's rich father might take Sara out of the school.

4
00:00:23.935 --> 00:00:29.910
So the headmistress always praised Sara for her good manners and kindness to the other girls.

5
00:00:29.911 --> 00:00:33.639
She always let Sara do whatever she liked.

6
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.036
And quiet Sara never did anything to break the rules.

7
00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:43.695
"Lots of things just happen by accident," Sara said to Ermengarde one day.

8
00:00:43.696 --> 00:00:47.314
"I'm just lucky that my father is kind and rich.

9
00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:50.416
I'm also lucky that I learn new things easily.

10
00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:55.826
Maybe," she went on thoughtfully, "I'm really an awful child.

11
00:00:55.827 --> 00:00:59.814
But I'll never know because I don't have any problems."

12
00:00:59.815 --> 00:01:05.183
"Lavinia doesn't have any problems, and she's horrid!" said Ermengarde.

13
00:01:05.184 --> 00:01:08.520
Sara rubbed her nose as she considered this.

14
00:01:08.521 --> 00:01:13.659
Then she tried to be kind by repeating something she'd heard Miss Amelia say.

15
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:18.833
"Maybe Lavinia is horrid because she's growing so fast."

16
00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:22.979
But Sara had to admit that Lavinia was indeed horrid.

17
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.470
Lavinia was also jealous of Sara.

18
00:01:26.471 --> 00:01:33.361
Before Sara came, Lavinia had been the best-dressed girl at school and Miss Minchin's favorite.

19
00:01:33.362 --> 00:01:37.822
She ruled over the older girls and scared the younger ones.

20
00:01:37.823 --> 00:01:42.170
All the girls followed her because they were afraid not to.

21
00:01:42.171 --> 00:01:47.682
But then Sara arrived. Although Sara was rich, she was friendly.

22
00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:52.803
And as time went on, the other girls began to follow her because they liked her.

23
00:01:52.804 --> 00:01:57.024
The youngest girls adored her because she was kind to them.

24
00:01:57.025 --> 00:02:01.424
She hosted tea parties in her room and introduced them to Emily.

25
00:02:01.425 --> 00:02:07.702
Unlike Sara, Lavinia was rarely kind to the younger girls.

26
00:02:07.703 --> 00:02:13.609
One morning Sara heard Lottie crying and shouting in the main sitting room.

27
00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:18.203
Lottie was four years old, the youngest girl at school.

28
00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:21.648
Lottie's father had spoiled her after her mother died.

29
00:02:21.649 --> 00:02:25.509
If Lottie wanted something, she cried until she got it.

30
00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:30.991
If she didn't want to do something, she threw a tantrum.

31
00:02:30.992 --> 00:02:35.450
Miss Minchin and Miss Amelia were trying to calm Lottie down.

32
00:02:35.451 --> 00:02:41.159
"Why is she upset now?" Miss Minchin yelled over the noise.

33
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:49.477
"Oh . . . oh . . . oh," sobbed Lottie. "I don't have a mama."

34
00:02:49.478 --> 00:02:53.658
"Don't cry, darling," said Miss Amelia.

35
00:02:53.659 --> 00:02:58.263
"Haven't got a mama!" howled Lottie.

36
00:02:58.264 --> 00:03:03.675
"You only say that when you can't have your way," said Miss Minchin.

37
00:03:03.676 --> 00:03:07.334
"You really should be whipped, you naughty child."

38
00:03:07.335 --> 00:03:13.709
Lottie wailed louder than ever. Miss Amelia began to cry.

39
00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:20.002
Miss Minchin got so angry, she stormed out of the room and left her sister to deal with the problem.

40
00:03:20.003 --> 00:03:22.396
Sara was standing in the hallway.

41
00:03:22.397 --> 00:03:28.392
"Oh, Sara!" Miss Minchin forced herself to give Sara a nice smile.

42
00:03:28.393 --> 00:03:35.035
"I stopped because I heard Lottie," said Sara. "Perhaps I could help her?"

43
00:03:35.036 --> 00:03:38.519
Miss Minchin's expression changed slightly.

44
00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:43.038
"You are a clever child," she said in a sharp tone.

45
00:03:43.039 --> 00:03:45.845
Then she softened her voice.

46
00:03:45.846 --> 00:03:51.610
"Go ahead. You can't do any worse than my sister is doing."

47
00:03:51.611 --> 00:03:56.394
Sara entered the room and found Lottie kicking and screaming on the floor.

48
00:03:56.395 --> 00:04:00.787
Miss Amelia was bending over her, looking hot and tired.

49
00:04:00.788 --> 00:04:05.905
"Poor darling," murmured Miss Amelia a few times.

50
00:04:05.906 --> 00:04:12.398
Then she said in quite a different tone, "Stop it, Lottie! You're a wicked child!"

51
00:04:12.399 --> 00:04:15.813
"Miss Amelia," Sara said quietly.

52
00:04:15.814 --> 00:04:19.816
"Miss Minchin says I may try to make her stop."

53
00:04:19.817 --> 00:04:22.479
Miss Amelia turned and looked at her.

54
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:30.752
"Oh, do you think you can?" she gasped. "Lottie is such a dreadful child."

55
00:04:30.753 --> 00:04:37.711
"If you'll quietly leave the room, I'll see what I can do," promised Sara.

56
00:04:37.712 --> 00:04:42.224
Miss Amelia slipped out, leaving the two girls alone.

57
00:04:42.225 --> 00:04:46.861
Sara said nothing and she did nothing.

58
00:04:46.862 --> 00:04:50.632
She simply sat quietly on the floor next to Lottie.

59
00:04:50.633 --> 00:04:56.432
Lottie didn't know what was going on. She looked up at Sara.

60
00:04:56.433 --> 00:05:04.047
"I . . . haven't . . . got a . . . mama," she tried to wail.

61
00:05:04.048 --> 00:05:07.431
"Neither do I," said Sara.

62
00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:13.188
This was so surprising that Lottie sat up. "Where is your mama?"

63
00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:18.239
"Both our mamas are angels in heaven," Sara answered.

64
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.963
"Should I tell you about heaven?"

65
00:05:20.964 --> 00:05:25.325
Lottie dried her tears. "Yes, please."

66
00:05:25.326 --> 00:05:32.813
Sara told her a story of a beautiful place filled with happy angels and fields of flowers.

67
00:05:32.814 --> 00:05:37.932
"But I don't have a mama here at this school!" said Lottie.

68
00:05:37.933 --> 00:05:43.600
Sara reached for Lottie's hand. "I'll be your mama," she said.

69
00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:46.697
"And Emily will be your sister."

70
00:05:46.698 --> 00:05:51.593
Lottie smiled happily. "Let's go tell Emily."

71
00:05:51.594 --> 00:05:56.491
"Yes, and then I'll brush your hair for you," added Sara.

72
00:05:56.492 --> 00:06:01.105
Lottie happily agreed and trotted upstairs after Sara.

73
00:06:01.106 --> 00:06:11.059
By now Lottie had completely forgotten what had first upset her—Miss Amelia had tried to brush her hair!
